-$$\frac12\sum_{i+j=k}ijc_ic_j=\frac{q^k}{t^2}[z^k]\frac{T(z)^2}{2}=\frac{k-1}{t}c_k,$$
-because $U=T-T^2/2$ implies $[z^k]T^2/2=(k-1)a_k$. The loss is $kc_kM_1=kc_k$ by step 1.1. Their difference is exactly $\dot c_k$, verifying every coefficient equation. As $t\downarrow0$, $c_1(t)\to1$ and $c_k(t)\to0$ for $k\ge2$, so the initial data hold. [F1, step 1.1, algebra]
